{title: Red River Valley}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: G}

{c: Verse 1}
From this [G]valley they say you are [C]going,
We will [G]miss your bright eyes and sweet [D7]smile,
For they [G]say you are taking the [C]sunshine,
That has [G]brightened our [D7]pathway a[G]while.

{c: Chorus}
Come and [G]sit by my side if you [C]love me,
Do not [G]hasten to bid me a[D7]dieu,
But re[G]member the Red River [C]Valley,
And the [G]cowboy who [D7]loved you so [G]true.
